#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083004 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083203 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c47216a0-3e51-50bb-b7eb-f92592db5dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial Using Synthetic Division"}] :question/id #uuid "551cceca-a69f-57c1-b4b0-c8f7aedd3cdc" :question/math-academy-id "e-5146" :question/problem "Use synthetic division to divide $5x^4+x^3+6x+2$ by $x+1$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing an $x^2$ term, so we insert a $0x^2$ in its place and carry out the process in the same way.\n\n$$\n-1\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix}2; - 5\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}2 \\mid 0\n$$\n\nSince the remainder is $0$, it means that $x+1$ divides $5x^4+x^3+6x+2$ exactly and gives a quotient of $5x^3-4x^2+4x+2$.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x^4+x^3+6x+2}{x+1} = 5x^3-4x^2+4x+2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083005 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083204 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b0a87cd-e9b5-5ca1-8132-b62a715264ac" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial With Leading Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "6d179766-30a7-5cd9-ba38-2ee6f49d37b8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5149" :question/problem "Find the quotient and remainder of $\\dfrac{3x^4+7x^3-10x+8}{2-3x}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the divisor in standard form as $-3x+2$. Then, we factor out the leading coefficient. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3x^{4} + 7x^{3} - 10x + 8}{-3x + 2} &= (3x^{4} + 7x^{3} - 10x + 8)/(-3(x - \\frac{2}{3})) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}((3x^{4} + 7x^{3} - 10x + 8)/((x - \\frac{2}{3})))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process on\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^4+7x^3-10x+8}{\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)}\n$$\n\nremembering to include a coefficient of zero for the $x^2$ term, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 7 & 0 & -10\\end{vmatrix}8; 2\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{vmatrix}- 6 \\mid 4\n$$\n\nReading off the bottom row, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x^4+7x^3-10x+8}{\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)} = 3x^3+9x^2+6x-6+\\frac{4}{\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply by the original\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac 1 3\n$$\n\nfactor to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3x^{4} + 7x^{3} - 10x + 8}{2 - 3x} &= -\\frac{1}{3}(3x^{3} + 9x^{2} + 6x - 6 + (4)/((x - \\frac{2}{3}))) \\\\\n&=-x^{3} - 3x^{2} - 2x + 2 + \\frac{4}{2 - 3x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083204 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b0a87cd-e9b5-5ca1-8132-b62a715264ac" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial With Leading Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf342cce-75a0-51e5-9b74-c5d653177672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x - 1 + \\frac{5}{6x - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080668} {:answer/id #uuid "d22cf791-52e9-5269-8cd4-cad1a2a203fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x + 5 + \\frac{5}{6x - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080669} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b5ef42-0f76-5261-8d6b-49743c2dd842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x - \\frac{5}{6x - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080670} {:answer/id #uuid "500544a5-781b-51be-b813-39a7dfacf8f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x + 1 + \\frac{5}{6x - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080671} {:answer/id #uuid "6c27c605-0e52-5252-a210-639d84364b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x + 2 + \\frac{5}{6x - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080672}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6ea95026-8e39-5cf6-afd5-80e17b2a0504" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :